<!--
  The same nine cells for Android 13+ themed icons — same geometry as ic_launcher_foreground, see
  the note there for why the grid is 46 across and not 60.

  A monochrome layer is a mask: the system supplies the colour from the user's wallpaper theme and
  keeps only our alpha. So the kept days are opaque and the three unkept ones hold the same 0.28
  that separates them in the colour version — the shape survives the recolour, the meaning with it.

  Kept as its own file rather than aliasing the foreground: that one names a colour resource, and a
  themed icon must not carry the app's blue into the user's palette.
-->
